      "text": "To determine the value of \\( n \\) that makes the seven-digit number \\( 854n526 \\) divisible by 11, we can use the divisibility rule for 11. According to this rule, a number is divisible by 11 if the difference between the sum of the digits in the odd positions and the sum of the digits in the even positions is a multiple of 11 (including 0).\n\nFor the number \\( 854n526 \\), the digits in the odd positions are \\( 8, 4, 5, 6 \\) and the digits in the even positions are \\( 5, n, 2 \\). We calculate the sums of these digits as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of digits in odd positions} = 8 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 23\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{Sum of digits in even positions} = 5 + n + 2 = 7 + n\n\\]\n\nAccording to the divisibility rule, the difference between these sums must be a multiple of 11:\n\n\\[\n23 - (7 + n) = 16 - n\n\\]\n\nThis difference must be a multiple of 11. Therefore, we need:\n\n\\[\n16 - n = 11 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad 16 - n = -11\n\\]\n\nSolving the first equation:\n\n\\[\n16 - n = 11 \\implies n = 16 - 11 \\implies n = 5\n\\]\n\nSolving the second equation:\n\n\\[\n16 - n = -11 \\implies n = 16 + 11 \\implies n = 27\n\\]\n\nSince \\( n \\) must be a digit (i.e., an integer between 0 and 9), we discard \\( n = 27 \\) and accept \\( n = 5 \\).\n\nThus, the value of \\( n \\) that makes the number \\( 854n526 \\) divisible by 11 is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
